From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Faris Benhaddou <farisbenhaddou@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:50:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] audren: merge updates closer than a frame for a renderer
 without effects

Bink's sound (Assassin's Creed Brotherhood's opening Previously_On.bk2, a
renderer with 0 effects) calls RequestUpdate many times per 5 ms while holding
its own lock. Each update took the catch-up path and, with the queue full,
waited ~5 ms for the render thread; the game's task thread waited on Bink's
lock, so the video ran at ~10 fps and its sound starved (887 of 24000 frames
not silent). With no effects there is nothing to initialize between updates,
so while one catch-up frame of that renderer is still queued the update
merges, as on hardware. Renderers with effects keep the catch-up behavior.

It changes when an update renders, so it is a profile key, audren_merge
(on / off, off by default): every game without the key keeps a catch-up
frame per update as before. The Ezio Collection's profile sets it.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1402
Reason: with audren_merge on, Brotherhood's opening video (Bink, a renderer with no effects) ran at about 10 fps with silent sound: its updates waited for catch-up frames it does not need
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#483
---
 dm/games/README.md            |  1 +
 dm/games/game.py              |  5 ++++-
 dm/host/hle_audren.c          | 14 +++++++++++---
 dm/host/hle_profile.c         | 12 ++++++++----
 dm/host/hle_profile.h         |  1 +
 dm/host/tests/t_audren_work.c |  2 ++
 6 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/README.md b/dm/games/README.md
index ae7dd45a..0029b1ae 100644
--- a/dm/games/README.md
+++ b/dm/games/README.md
@@ -235,6 +235,7 @@ One row per profile; the notes are each profile's `README.md`.
 | `tex_flush_upload` | `on` / `off` (the default): a texture the game fills from the CPU in place (no packaged layout, no `WriteTexels`) and publishes with `nvnMemoryPoolFlushMappedRange` is uploaded from guest memory like a packaged one, and re-uploaded when its pages change (`ft_add` in `hle_nvn.c`). Tears of the Kingdom streams all its textures this way; without it the 3D scene is black. Off by default because a flushed range in another game could cover an image a shader writes, whose GPU content the upload would replace. Without the key, every game still gets a texture's storage once when the game flushed it before the texture's first use (`nvn_flushed` in `hle_nvn.c`: Breath of the Wild's sky tables); the key is for textures the CPU writes again after that |
 | `render_cond` | `on` / `off` (the default): `SetRenderEnableConditional` / `SetRenderEnable` are recorded and evaluated at replay, and a timestamp report's counter field is 0 as on the GPU (`OP_RENDER_COND` in `nvn_mtl.m`). Tears of the Kingdom wraps its clears in conditions that skip clearing a target nothing has drawn into since its last clear; without the key every clear runs and its 3D scene is black. Animal Crossing: New Horizons too: four clear-only passes wiped its composite before the window copy, and every frame was black. Off by default: other games draw everything, as before |
 | `tex_dirty_upload` | `on` / `off` (the default), needs `tex_flush_upload`: a registered texture whose pages the CPU writes after `nvnTextureInitialize` without any NVN flush is uploaded as well (its pages are write-protected at registration, checked on first use; `nvn_ft_written` in `hle_nvn.c`). Tears of the Kingdom fills its ASTC terrain material arrays this way; without it the cave is magenta. FINAL FANTASY TACTICS - The Ivalice Chronicles loads its UI textures straight into CPU-uncached pools, which need no flush, after creating them; without both keys its screen stays black. The Great Ace Attorney Chronicles copies every texture into a CPU-cached pool after creating it and never flushes (its `main` has no cache maintenance at all): black too |
+| `audren_merge` | `on` / `off` (the default): for an audio renderer with no effects, an update that comes before the render thread played the last catch-up frame merges with it, as on hardware, instead of rendering another one first (`hle_audren.c` `h_ars_Update`). For Bink videos that update many times per frame under their own lock (Assassin's Creed Brotherhood's opening, The Ezio Collection): without it each update waited about 5 ms for the render thread, and the video ran at about 10 fps with silent sound |
 | `tex_dyn_slots` | `on` / `off` (the default): a shader whose buffer-texture handle the translator could not trace to one slot gets Ryujinx's fallback arrays (`<stage>_<tb|s>_cb0_40000000`: 32 buffer textures and samplers indexed by the handle's texture / sampler ID; any other sampled texture indexes the whole pool without a key, [Texture handles from game memory index the pools](../../docs/reference/shaders.md#texture-handles-from-game-memory-index-the-pools)). With the key the replay puts slot indices in that shader's c2 texture and sampler tables (texture slot r → r, sampler slot r → r << 20) and binds slot k at element k, so the shader's own arithmetic picks the binding (`NVN_RB_TEXD` / `NVN_RB_SAMPD` in `nvn_mtl.m`). Right only where the handle comes from c2's tables: Octopath Traveler 0's 61 such vertex shaders read separate texture slots 0-10 and samplers 0-4 there and nothing else (FINAL FANTASY RESONANCE's 2,077 the texture table words 0x168-0x1c0 and sampler table words 0x568-0x590). Off, such shaders do not load. Not part of the shader chain version |
 | `gpu_timestamps` | What a timestamp report (`nvnCommandBufferReportCounter`) records: `submission` (the default) = the time the whole submission completed, the same for every report in it; `segment` = the GPU start (`TIMESTAMP_TOP`) or end (the other types) of the segment the report was encoded in (the host commits a submission in segments of 64 draws, `sub_cut` in `nvn_mtl.m`), so two reports of one submission bracket the GPU time between them, as on hardware. Breath of the Wild needs `segment`: its frame-interval controller and its dynamic resolution read the GPU time between the frame's first and last report, and with one time for both they read 0 (the game kept 60 fps in slow motion when the GPU could not keep up). `DM_NVN_GPU_TS=segment` / `submission` overrides it, also from `Documents/env.txt` |
 | `vconv_range` | `on` / `off` (the default): vertex attributes the replay converts on the CPU (integer shader inputs fed float-type formats and the like, `vconv_bind` in `nvn_mtl.m`) are converted only over the vertices each draw reads (first / count, or the smallest and largest index of a direct indexed draw, kept while the index pages stay unwritten) instead of the whole bound range. Age of Calamity binds whole mesh pools: in a battle that was millions of vertices a frame. Indirect draws, per-instance streams and indices with a GPU write queued on them keep the whole range. `DM_NVN_VCONV_CHECK=1` scans the indices again at every reuse and reports differences; `DM_NVN_VCONV_RANGE=0` / `1` overrides it |
diff --git a/dm/games/game.py b/dm/games/game.py
index b6e546a2..5795ade7 100644
--- a/dm/games/game.py
+++ b/dm/games/game.py
@@ -195,6 +195,8 @@ def header_one(g):
     if rcd not in ('on', 'off'): sys.exit(f'{g.id}: render_cond must be on or off: {rcd}')
     tfu = g.get('tex_flush_upload', 'off')   # textures written by the CPU into a pool and published with nvnMemoryPoolFlushMappedRange are uploaded like packaged ones (hle_nvn.c): on / off
     if tfu not in ('on', 'off'): sys.exit(f'{g.id}: tex_flush_upload must be on or off: {tfu}')
+    arm = g.get('audren_merge', 'off')   # audren: updates closer than a frame merge for a renderer with no effects (hle_audren.c h_ars_Update): on / off
+    if arm not in ('on', 'off'): sys.exit(f'{g.id}: audren_merge must be on or off: {arm}')
     tdu = g.get('tex_dirty_upload', 'off')   # with tex_flush_upload: a registered texture the CPU writes after init without any flush is uploaded too (dirty pages, hle_nvn.c nvn_ft_written): on / off
     if tdu not in ('on', 'off') or (tdu == 'on' and tfu != 'on'): sys.exit(f'{g.id}: tex_dirty_upload must be on or off, and needs tex_flush_upload on: {tdu}')
     tbc = g.get('tex_bc_cpu', 'off')   # decode BC-compressed textures on the CPU when the GPU has no BC support (A15/A16 and older; nvn_mtl.m uses nvn_bcdec.c): on / off
@@ -260,6 +262,7 @@ def header_one(g):
          f'#define DM_GAME_SHADER_KEY_SKIP_OFF {sko:#x}', f'#define DM_GAME_SHADER_KEY_SKIP_LEN {skl:#x}',
          f'#define DM_GAME_RENDER_COND {int(rcd == "on")}',
          f'#define DM_GAME_TEX_DIRTY_UPLOAD {int(tdu == "on")}',
+         f'#define DM_GAME_AUDREN_MERGE {int(arm == "on")}',
          f'#define DM_GAME_TEX_BC_CPU {int(tbc == "on")}',
          f'#define DM_GAME_TEX_DYN_SLOTS {int(tds == "on")}',
          f'#define DM_GAME_GPU_TS_SEGMENT {int(gts == "segment")}',
@@ -292,7 +295,7 @@ if __name__ == '__main__':
                 ('fps_target', 'FPS_TARGET'), ('fps_hold', 'FPS_HOLD'), ('present_snap', 'PRESENT_SNAP'), ('pso_mtl4', 'PSO_MTL4'),
                 ('shared_font', 'SHARED_FONT_TTF'), ('pad_layout', 'PAD_LAYOUT'), ('op_mode', 'OPMODE'), ('perf_mode', 'PERF_BOOST'),
                 ('feedback_snap', 'FEEDBACK_SNAP'), ('tex_flush_upload', 'TEX_FLUSH_UPLOAD'), ('render_cond', 'RENDER_COND'),
-                ('tex_dirty_upload', 'TEX_DIRTY_UPLOAD'), ('tex_dyn_slots', 'TEX_DYN_SLOTS'), ('gpu_timestamps', 'GPU_TS_SEGMENT'),
+                ('tex_dirty_upload', 'TEX_DIRTY_UPLOAD'), ('audren_merge', 'AUDREN_MERGE'), ('tex_dyn_slots', 'TEX_DYN_SLOTS'), ('gpu_timestamps', 'GPU_TS_SEGMENT'),
                 ('vconv_range', 'VCONV_RANGE'), ('stdalloc_cap', 'STDALLOC_CAP'), ('tex_bc_cpu', 'TEX_BC_CPU'), ('ue_texture_pool', 'UE_TEXTURE_POOL'),
                 ('enc_thread', 'ENC_THREAD'), ('game_args', 'ARGS'), ('game_env', 'ENV')]
         def val(macro):   # the header's C spelling → the file's plain spelling
diff --git a/dm/host/hle_audren.c b/dm/host/hle_audren.c
index 3b074d78..3491de93 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_audren.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_audren.c
@@ -95,6 +95,8 @@ typedef struct {
     void *render_tt;                         // the render thread (ThreadType from dm_guest_thread_spawn): Close joins it before the SDK tears the renderer down
     int16_t frame[FRAME_MAX * 2]; int frame_n;   // the latest frame (stereo int16)
     _Atomic uint64_t frames, nonsilent, updates, renders, catchups;
+    int effects;                             // its effect count (AudioRendererParameter +0x18): with none, updates closer than a frame merge (h_ars_Update)
+    _Atomic uint64_t merged;                 // updates that merged with a queued catch-up frame instead of rendering one
     uint64_t last_r; int updated;            // the render count at the last update, once there was one
     int16_t cq[CQ][FRAME_MAX * 2]; int cq_n[CQ]; _Atomic uint32_t cq_head, cq_tail;   // output queue of catch-up frames
     pthread_mutex_t cq_mu; pthread_cond_t cq_cv;   // the render thread signals each frame it takes off the queue (catch-up pacing)
@@ -233,7 +235,7 @@ static Result ar_open(void **handle, void *ev, const uint8_t *param, void *work,
     if (a) {   // the slot's old contents are of a closed renderer, whose thread has ended; memset leaves no lock held
         memset(a, 0, sizeof *a);
         pthread_mutex_init(&a->cq_mu, NULL); pthread_cond_init(&a->cq_cv, NULL);
-        a->handle[0] = handle[0]; a->handle[1] = handle[1]; atomic_store(&a->open, 1);
+        a->handle[0] = handle[0]; a->handle[1] = handle[1]; a->effects = *(int32_t *)(param + 0x18); atomic_store(&a->open, 1);
     }
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_ar_mu);
     LOG("audren: renderer %d opened from %s+%#llx", a ? ar_index(a) : -1, m ? m->name : "host", m ? (unsigned long long)((uint8_t *)ra - m->base) : 0ULL);
@@ -494,7 +496,7 @@ static Result render_once(ar_t *a, uint8_t *sys, int16_t *dst, int *nout) {
     if (dst) *nout = capture(a, cl, n, dst);
     // render time per frame (budget: 5 ms per frame): mean / max every 2000 frames
     static uint64_t sum, mx, cnt; uint64_t d = now_ns() - t0; sum += d; if (d > mx) mx = d;
-    if (++cnt == 2000) { LOG("audren: render time mean %.2f ms / max %.2f ms (5 ms budget per frame, last 2000 frames); catch-up renders so far %llu", sum / 2000 / 1e6, mx / 1e6, (unsigned long long)atomic_load(&a->catchups)); sum = mx = cnt = 0; }
+    if (++cnt == 2000) { LOG("audren: render time mean %.2f ms / max %.2f ms (5 ms budget per frame, last 2000 frames); catch-up renders so far %llu, updates merged %llu", sum / 2000 / 1e6, mx / 1e6, (unsigned long long)atomic_load(&a->catchups), (unsigned long long)atomic_load(&a->merged)); sum = mx = cnt = 0; }
     pthread_mutex_unlock(&g_render_mu);
     return RES_OK;
 }
@@ -548,7 +550,13 @@ HLE_FORCE("_ZN2nn5audio6server17AudioRenderSystem6UpdateEPvmS3_mPKvm", "renderer
     ar_t *a = ar_of_sys(sys);
     if (!a) return orig(sys, o, on, p, pn, in, inn);   // two renderers just opened, neither has rendered: at most one catch-up frame less
     uint64_t u = atomic_fetch_add(&a->updates, 1) + 1, r = atomic_load(&a->renders);
-    if (a->updated && r == a->last_r) {
+    // A renderer without effects needs no frame between two updates (that is only for an effect's initialization, above), and on hardware updates closer than 5 ms simply merge.
+    // Bink's sound (Assassin's Creed Brotherhood's Previously_On.bk2, 0 effects) updates many times per 5 ms from two threads while holding its own lock: each update past a full
+    // queue waited ~5 ms for the render thread, the game's task thread waited on Bink's lock, and the video ran at ~10 fps with silent sound. One unplayed catch-up frame queued is enough there.
+    // Only where the profile asks (audren_merge on): every other game keeps a catch-up frame per update
+    int merge = dm_profile()->audren_merge && !a->effects && atomic_load(&a->cq_tail) != atomic_load(&a->cq_head);
+    if (a->updated && r == a->last_r && merge) atomic_fetch_add(&a->merged, 1);
+    else if (a->updated && r == a->last_r) {
         uint64_t c = atomic_fetch_add(&a->catchups, 1) + 1;
         if (c <= 3) LOG("audren: renderer %d: no frame rendered before update %llu, rendering a catch-up frame first (%llu so far)", ar_index(a), (unsigned long long)u, (unsigned long long)c);
         uint32_t t = atomic_load(&a->cq_tail);
